    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/Senior-Manager--Technical-and-Scientific-Services_R-69406-1": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Technical and Scientific Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nSchool of Agriculture and Food Sustainability. Full-time, continuing position. Base salary will be in the range $140,766 to $148,862 plus 17% super (HEW Level 9). Based at our St Lucia and Gatton Campus – take a  virtual tour !    About This Opportunity The Senior Manager, Technical & Scientific Services provides strategic leadership across two critical service streams within the School of Agriculture and Food Sustainability. You will lead a diverse, multidisciplinary team delivering scientific, laboratory, technical and operational services across UQ’s St Lucia and Gatton campuses. Working collaboratively with academic leaders, researchers and professional colleagues, you will shape a coordinated, whole-of-School approach to laboratory operations, field services, teaching support, research infrastructure, equipment investment and service improvement. This is a purposeful leadership opportunity to strengthen operational excellence while enabling high-quality teaching and research outcomes.   Key responsibilities will include: Provide strategic leadership and operational management for the School’s Technical and Scientific Services teams, building a positive, inclusive and accountable culture. Develop and implement a coordinated, whole-of-School approach to technical and scientific services, including teaching support resources, research infrastructure, fieldwork planning and equipment investment. Drive continuous improvement across laboratory access, safety, compliance, quality assurance, service delivery and sustainable scientific operations. Provide strategic and operational advice to the School Executive, oversee portfolio budgets and build effective relationships with academic, professional and external stakeholders.   About You Postgraduate qualifications together with significant relevant experience in scientific, laboratory or research service delivery, or an equivalent combination of relevant education, training and experience. Demonstrated experience in organic and/or inorganic chemistry analytical laboratories and broad technical, analytical and scientific knowledge across a range of disciplines, with exposure to agricultural, food, plant, soil, animal and environmental sciences. Demonstrated experience leading multidisciplinary teams in complex teaching, research, laboratory or field-based environments. High-level people, project and resource management capability, including the ability to motivate staff, strengthen team cohesion and foster clear communication. Strong operational judgement and the ability to translate strategic priorities into practical, coordinated and sustainable services. Experience in budget planning, financial oversight, quality assurance, compliance, risk management and workplace health and safety. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with a proven ability to build collaborative relationships with academic, professional and external stakeholders. A commitment to client service, continuous improvement, research integrity, ethics, openness, respect and inclusion. Capacity to work across both the St Lucia and Gatton campuses, including travelling between locations.   About UQ As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a visionary and collaborative community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of benefits and rewards are available, such as:   Free parking and an intercampus bus - Gatton Campus On-campus childcare , a medical clinic and a post office. Up to 26 weeks of paid parental leave or paid primary care leave. 17% super and 17.5% annual leave loading. Health and wellness discounts, including Fitness Passport access, free annual flu vaccinations, discounted health insurance and access to the Employee Assistance Program for staff and their immediate family. Career development opportunities, including access to exclusive internal-only vacancies and the Study for Staff program. A 25% discount on eligible UQ Vets services. Access to the $4.1 million UQ Sports facility .   Interested? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Felicity Ray at f.ray@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number below in the subject line.   When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume and cover letter summarising how your background aligns with the ‘About You’ section. Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted.   Other Information Pre-employment checks may include verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, criminal history checks and mandatory immunisations. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer-sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.   We’re dedicated to equity, diversity and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criterion but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au or calling +61 7 3365 2623.   Applications close Sunday 18 October 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-69406)."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/Facilities-and-Infrastructure-Manager--Research-_R-69518-1": {
      "title": "Facilities and Infrastructure Manager (Research)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nQueensland Alliance for Agriculture and Food Innovation . Full-time, continuing position. Base salary will be in the range $120,317 to $134,893 plus 17% super (HEW Level 8). Based primarily at our St Lucia location , with travel to other Brisbane and regional sites.   About This Opportunity Join the Queensland Alliance for Agriculture and Food Innovation and lead the facilities, infrastructure and asset services that enable high-impact agricultural and food research. Working across a geographically dispersed network of biological science laboratories, field facilities and shared government sites, you will provide strategic advice, lead a team of technical professionals and build collaborative relationships across UQ, the Queensland Government and external partners. This is a purposeful opportunity to shape safe, reliable and future-ready research environments while contributing to a visionary and inclusive culture focused on creating change together.   This role will primarily be based at St Lucia campus but will include travel to other Brisbane and regional UQ and DAF sites such as Dutton Park, Coopers Plains, Gatton and Warwick.     Key responsibilities will include, but not limited to: Lead and develop QAAFI’s health, safety and facilities team, in collaboration with QAAFI’s Health, Safety and Wellness Manager, providing strategic direction, performance leadership and operational oversight to ensure the delivery of high-quality facilities and infrastructure services that support world-class agricultural and food research. Coordinate the planning, delivery and continuous improvement of facilities and infrastructure programs, including policy development, capital and minor works projects, stakeholder engagement, operational planning and service enhancement across multiple UQ and partner sites. Manage complex infrastructure and facilities operations, overseeing maintenance, upgrades, space planning, specialised research environments, centrally managed equipment and critical response activities to ensure safe, compliant and effective research facilities. Provide strategic leadership in asset, financial and resource management, including asset lifecycle planning, equipment replacement programs, stocktakes, budgeting, forecasting and the stewardship of infrastructure and facilities-related expenditure. Build strong partnerships and ensure service excellence, collaborating with academic, research, professional and external stakeholders to deliver stakeholder-focused outcomes, maintain regulatory compliance, support health and safety requirements, and monitor key performance metrics to drive continuous improvement.   About You Postgraduate qualifications, or progress towards postgraduate qualifications, with extensive relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant education, training and experience. Proven capability in leading and developing professional teams, building capacity and embedding a values-based culture of service innovation, accountability and continuous improvement. Demonstrated experience implementing policies, procedures and systems relating to facilities, infrastructure or asset management. Working knowledge of university or scientific research facility operations, or the capacity to rapidly acquire this knowledge, including infrastructure projects, maintenance, security controls and regulatory requirements. Strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to negotiate, influence, provide strategic advice and build productive relationships with diverse internal and external stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to work autonomously, manage competing priorities and deliver accurate outcomes within required timeframes. Experience using a broad range of computer applications in a networked environment. A current Australian driver licence.   Experience managing scientific research facilities, particularly biological or agricultural facilities involving regulated laboratories, fieldwork, remote settings, biosecurity or other regulatory requirements, will be highly regarded.   About UQ As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a visionary and collaborative community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of benefits and rewards are available. Enjoy up to 26 weeks paid parental and primary care leave, 17% super, 17.5% leave loading, flexible and hybrid working options, health and wellbeing programs, a heavily discounted Study for Staff program, on-campus childcare, affordable parking and salary packaging.   Interested? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Dr Rona Barugahare at r.barugahare@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number below in the subject line.   When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume and cover letter summarising how your background aligns with the ‘About You’ section. Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted.   Other Information Pre-employment checks may include verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, criminal history checks and mandatory immunisations. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer-sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.   We’re dedicated to equity, diversity and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criterion but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au or calling +61 7 3365 2623.   Applications close Sunday 18 October 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-69518)."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/Mater-Misericordiae-Hospitals--QCH-South-Brisbane/Manager--Network-Engagement-and-Communications_R-67895-1": {
      "title": "Manager, Network Engagement and Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nChild Health Research Centre . Part-time (60%), fixed-term position for up to two years. Base salary will be in the range $120,317 to $134,893 + 17% super (HEW Level 8). Based at our Centre for Children’s Health Research, South Brisbane location. About This Opportunity Join the Child Health Research Centre as Manager, Network Engagement and Communications for the First 10K Days Child, Adolescent and Family Wellbeing Network. Working closely with the Network Convenor, leadership team and members, you will provide high-level strategic and operational leadership that turns priorities into purposeful initiatives, partnerships, events and communications. In this collaborative and inclusive environment, you will connect researchers, clinicians, policymakers, service providers, funders and community stakeholders, helping the Network exchange knowledge, translate research and create meaningful change for children, adolescents and families. Key responsibilities will include: Translate the Network’s strategic priorities into actionable workplans, deliverables, operational processes, milestone reports, briefs, communications and evaluation activities. Develop and implement an integrated communication and engagement approach that strengthens connections, collaboration, knowledge exchange, research translation and workforce capability across the Network. Build and sustain mutually beneficial relationships with researchers, partner organisations, clinicians, policymakers, service providers, funders and community stakeholders, while coordinating forums, training sessions, recognition events and partnership meetings. Collaborate with internal specialists to design and continuously improve practical, user-centred digital platforms, communication systems and engagement tools, while supporting effective governance, clear decision-making and sustainable partnerships. About You Demonstrated experience developing and implementing communication and engagement strategies within a large or complex organisation. Demonstrated ability to establish, manage and sustain positive relationships with diverse internal and external stakeholders, including researchers, partner organisations, policymakers, service providers, community stakeholders and funding partners. Experience contributing to communication, engagement, partnership or marketing solutions, including digital platforms, applications or other technology-enabled communication tools. Strong strategic and operational capability, with experience translating priorities into practical plans, deliverables, events, communications and measurable outcomes. Highly developed organisational, problem-solving and attention-to-detail skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deliver high-quality work. The ability to collaborate effectively with technical specialists, including information technology, digital, marketing and external vendors, to translate user needs into practical and intuitive solutions. About UQ As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of benefits and rewards are available. Enjoy up to 26 weeks paid parental and primary care leave, 17% super, 17.5% leave loading, flexible and hybrid working options, health and wellbeing programs, a heavily discounted Study for Staff program, on-campus childcare, affordable parking, and salary packaging. Interested? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Dr Annie Chen ( chrc.centremanager@uq.edu.au ). For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number below in the subject line. When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume and cover letter summarising how your background aligns to the ‘About You’ section. Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted. Other Information Pre-employment checks may include verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, criminal history checks and mandatory immunisations checks. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements. You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment. We're dedicated to equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criterion but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au or calling +61 7 3365 2623. Applications close Wednesday 21 October 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-67895). Please note that interviews have been tentatively scheduled for the week commencing 2nd November 2026."
